# 🤖 PyBot — AI Chatbot

PyBot is a simple AI-powered chatbot built with **Python and Streamlit**. It provides a clean web interface where users can interact with an AI assistant in real time.

This project was built to understand how a Python application can connect to an **LLM API**, send user messages, receive AI-generated responses, and display them through a web interface.

## ✨ Features

* 💬 Interactive chat interface
* 🤖 AI-generated responses
* 🧠 Conversation history during the session
* ⚡ Real-time response generation
* 🖥️ Simple web-based UI using Streamlit
* 🔐 API key handled through environment variables

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **Python**
* **Streamlit** — web interface
* **LLM API** — AI response generation
* **Git & GitHub** — version control

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
Pybot-Chatbot/
│
├── app.py
├── requirements.txt
├── .env
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

> `.env` should not be uploaded to GitHub because it contains the API key.

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/tan-can/PyBot-Chatbot.git
cd PyBot-Chatbot
```

### 2. Create a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate it on Windows:

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Add your API key

Create a `.env` file in the project directory:

```text
API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```

Do not commit this file to GitHub.

### 5. Run the application

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

The application will open in your browser.

## 🔄 How It Works

```text
User
  ↓
Streamlit Chat Interface
  ↓
Python Application
  ↓
LLM API
  ↓
AI-generated Response
  ↓
Streamlit Interface
  ↓
User
```

The application takes the user's message, sends it to the configured language model through an API request, receives the generated response, and displays it in the chat interface.

